#==[99999]-未知物品 Unknown Items==
# 新出的物品 —— 看到有这种颜色的物品，代表你的过滤器该更新了！
#
# THE SAFETY NET. Anything no rule above matched lands here: a new league item, a
# base we have not curated, a class whose category is still empty.
#
# It SHOWS, deliberately, at every strictness level. The rule this filter is built
# on is that a Hide must name what it hides (a Class or a BaseType), so nothing is
# ever hidden by accident and whatever falls through has to stay visible. In
# Ruthless a missed drop costs far more than a little noise.
#
# Styling and sound follow Sharket's own convention: bright green plate, and an
# alert that literally says "please update the filter". It is meant to be
# unmistakable rather than pretty - seeing one in game means that base wants a
# home in base_mapping.
#
# `Rarity > Unique` is a defensive first pass for any rarity tier GGG adds later,
# which would otherwise fall past every Rarity-gated rule in the tree.
#
# ⚠️ BLACK TEXT, NOT WHITE. The plate stays the loud green — that is the whole point —
# but white on `0 255 0` measures 1.37:1, the worst pair in the entire filter, so the
# one thing this block exists to tell you (WHICH item is uncurated) was the one thing
# you could not read. Black on the same green is 15.3:1 and costs the loudness nothing.

Show
    Rarity > Unique
    SetFontSize 45
    SetTextColor 0 0 0 255
    SetBorderColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBackgroundColor 0 255 0 255
    CustomAlertSound "Sharket掉落音效\拜托~更新一下过滤吧.mp3" 300
    PlayEffect Green
    MinimapIcon 0 Green Star

Show
    SetFontSize 45
    SetTextColor 0 0 0 255
    SetBorderColor 0 0 0 0
    SetBackgroundColor 0 255 0 255
    CustomAlertSound "Sharket掉落音效\拜托~更新一下过滤吧.mp3" 300
    PlayEffect Green
    MinimapIcon 0 Green Star
